# Planted bugs for the schema-compat model. Each one must make the named check miss its expectation.
run fv-alloy schema-compat.als
properties AllLivePairsCompatible_AdditiveWithGracePeriod AllLivePairsCompatible_NoRule
file schema-compat.als

mutation a field can be required the same version it is added, with no grace period
detects AllLivePairsCompatible_AdditiveWithGracePeriod
-   all v: Version | some v.prev implies v.prev.fields in v.fields
-   all v: Version | some v.prev implies v.required in v.prev.fields
+   all v: Version | some v.prev implies v.prev.fields in v.fields

mutation compatibility no longer checks the producer at all
detects AllLivePairsCompatible_NoRule
- pred Compatible[pv, cv: Version] { cv.required in pv.fields }
+ pred Compatible[pv, cv: Version] { cv.required in pv.fields + cv.fields }

harmless a comment on LiveTogether is reworded
- -- During a rolling deploy, the immediately adjacent version runs alongside
- -- the current one, in either direction, until the rollout finishes.
+ -- The version one step older or one step newer, the two that overlap
+ -- while a rolling deploy is in progress.
